  "id": "visual-adaptation",
  "term": "visual adaptation",
  "definition": "Visual adaptation is the set of changes in visual function that happen after exposure to an environment, helping the nervous system process visual information more efficiently or improving what a person can perceive. A common example is dark adaptation, in which low light exposure enables better seeing in dim conditions.",
